  "title": "2026-09-08-reflow-152600 · llm-inference-gateway",
  "description": "# LLM inference gateway\nRead left to right across identity/admission, preparation and tier routing, and hosted or self-hosted execution. Clients request a capability tier through one endpoint. Admission limits concurrency and token rate; queued work expires explicitly rather than being served late.\n\nPrompt context and safety policy precede cache lookup. Exact and deterministic near-match hits bypass backend execution. Misses route by residency, health, latency, queue depth and price. Attempts retain request identity and idempotency keys.\n\nThe middle band separates failures before and after token emission: retryable pre-token failures reselect within the tier with a fresh deadline; non-retryable failures return immediately. Once tokens have been emitted, failure is visible and preserves delivered tokens rather than silently failing over.\n\nLower control paths show circuit exclusion and probe recovery, followed by spend-driven degradation and rejection. Attempt usage feeds metering, billing and a redacted audit store. A small structured evaluation sample goes to an isolated shadow backend and cannot change the client response. Dashed arrows denote control, accounting and evaluation paths; green paths deliver responses and red paths mark failure or rejection.",
